# Local-dev vars for `wrangler dev`. Copy this file and fill in the one blank below.
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# Never commit .dev.vars. In production set secrets with `wrangler secret put <NAME>`
# instead; plain vars go in wrangler.jsonc.
#
# These two are all you need. The optional variables are in the README, under
# "Optional variables" - none of them are required to run the kit.

# ── The only thing you have to fill in ───────────────────────────────────────
# Your org API key (`zct_…`), issued from the org admin surface. The plaintext is shown
# exactly once when it is created.
#
# SECURITY: this authenticates the Worker as your whole organization. It must never
# reach the browser, a log, or a client bundle.
ZOOCLAW_API_KEY=

# ── Local identity ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stands in for Cloudflare Access so you are signed in locally. Any string works; it is
# the key your chats are stored under. Never set this in production - without it, and
# without Access configured, every request is rejected, which is the behaviour you want.
DEV_EMAIL=you@example.com
